{"command": "cd /testbed && cat > specs/001-transactions/data-model.md <<'EOF'\n# Phase 1 Data Model: Batch Journal Writer for TinyDB\n\nFeature: `specs/001-transactions/spec.md` | Date: 2026-10-17\n\n## Entities\n\n### BatchWriter\n\n- **Represents**: The additive wrapper bound to exactly one `TinyDB` instance (spec entity `BatchWriter`).\n- **Fields**:\n  - `db`: the supplied `TinyDB` instance (never mutated structurally; ordinary APIs untouched).\n  - `table`: the default table handle, obtained once via `db.table(db.default_table_name)`.\n- **Behavior**: single method `apply(operations: list[dict]) -> list[int]`.\n- **State transitions**: stateless between calls; all state lives in the storage.\n\n### Operation (input, not persisted)\n\n- **Represents**: One change in a batch (spec entity `Operation`).\n- **Valid shapes** (validated before any mutation; violations raise `ValueError`):\n  - `{'op': 'insert', 'document': <dict>}` - `document` MUST be a `Mapping`; extra keys ignored (A5).\n  - `{'op': 'remove', 'doc_id': <int>}` - `doc_id` MUST be an `int` (bool excluded), `> 0` (A2); extra keys ignored.\n- **Invalid shapes**: non-dict entry; `op` missing or not in `{'insert','remove'}`; insert without `document` or with non-Mapping `document`; remove without `doc_id` or with non-int/bool/non-positive `doc_id`.\n\n### Document (persisted in default table)\n\n- **Represents**: A stored record (spec entity `Document`), key = positive integer ID, value = dict.\n- **Storage layout** (unchanged, existing TinyDB format):\n  `{table_name: {str(doc_id): dict}}` under the single storage root dict.\n- **ID assignment**: empty table -> first insert gets ID 1; otherwise `max(existing ids) + 1`, computed against the in-batch working dict (matches `Table._get_next_id`, tinydb/table.py:751).\n- **Aliasing rule (R03)**: stored value is `copy.deepcopy(document)` taken before the batch commits; the result list contains IDs only, so no document object is ever returned.\n\n## Relationships\n\n- `BatchWriter` 1..1 `TinyDB` instance; 1..1 default `Table`; `Table` 1..1 `Storage`.\n- A batch is a sequence of `Operation`s applied to the default table only; other tables in the storage root are carried through unchanged.\n\n## Validation Rules (from spec FR-005/FR-007)\n\n1. `operations` MUST be a list of dicts (non-list input is malformed -> `ValueError`).\n2. Every operation MUST match a valid shape above, else `ValueError`.\n3. A remove whose `doc_id` is not present in the working table when its turn arrives is an error -> `ValueError` (R02), which triggers rollback.\n4. Sequential semantics: an earlier insert in the same batch makes its ID removable by a later remove (A6).\n\n## State Transitions (default table)\n\n```\npre-batch snapshot S0\n  -> validate all operations (no mutation yet)\n  -> apply sequentially on working dict S1..Sn (in memory only)\n  -> on success: storage.write(working tables)         [committed]\n  -> on any error: storage.write(deepcopy(S0))          [rolled back]\n```\n\nObservable invariants:\n- After success: table equals the result of applying the operations to S0; IDs returned in insertion order.\n- After rollback: table is byte-for-byte equal to S0 (contents, IDs, order) (A7).\n- Previously acquired handles always re-read storage on `all()`/`__iter__`/`__len__`, so they observe either outcome (tinydb/table.py:715,771).\nEOF\ngrep -c '###' specs/001-transactions/data-model.md && echo DM_OK", "exit_code": 0, "stderr": "", "stdout": "3\nDM_OK\n"}